{"name":"Hot Toddy","hex":"#a7752c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hot toddy","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A drink made from alcoholic liquor (usually whisky) mixed with sugar, spice and hot water."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hot_toddy"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hot toddy","blocks":[{"text":"A hot toddy, also known as hot whiskey in Ireland, and occasionally called southern cough syrup within the Southern United States, is typically a mixed drink made of liquor and water with honey, lemon, and spices, and served hot. Recipes vary, and hot toddy is traditionally drunk as a nightcap before retiring for the night, in wet or cold weather, or to relieve the symptoms of the cold and flu. In How to Drink, Victoria Moore describes the drink as \"the vitamin C for health, the honey to soothe, the alcohol to numb.\""}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Hot_toddy_%281%29.jpg/330px-Hot_toddy_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hot_toddy","wikidata":"Q1418227"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Information_board_about_Ye_Olde_Red_Cow_pub_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1127950.jpg/500px-Information_board_about_Ye_Olde_Red_Cow_pub_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1127950.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Information_board_about_Ye_Olde_Red_Cow_pub_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1127950.jpg/500px-Information_board_about_Ye_Olde_Red_Cow_pub_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1127950.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Information board highlighting the hot toddy at Ye Olde Red Cow pub in London","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AInformation_board_about_Ye_Olde_Red_Cow_pub_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1127950.jpg"}],"sounds":{"hot toddy":[{"type":"audio/wav","src